Subject: vkd3d-shader: Support legacy HLSL function target qualifiers.

D3DX SDKs through 36 accept target-qualified overloads such as vs_1_1 and
ps_2_0. Keep their declarations distinct and select the matching target,
then the stage-wide qualifier, then an unqualified fallback. Type overload
ranking takes precedence. Preserve errors for qualifiers outside functions
and for modern compiler versions. Reset the current function after parsing
it so global initializers use the compilation target.

Based on Wine 36b6a2cf679. Native SDKs 30 and 36 establish the expected
success/failure and executable shader output. SDKs 37 and 43 verify the
modern behavior. Run make smoke-shaders for both architectures.

